---
import Footer from "~/components/Footer.astro";
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Footer demo" noIndex>
	<Footer slot="footer" count={247} lang="en-GB" />

	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
		<p class="font-display text-kicker tracking-kicker text-ink-3 uppercase">demo</p>
		<h1 class="font-display text-h1 tracking-display mt-2">Site footer</h1>
		<p class="text-body text-ink-2 mt-4 max-w-prose">
			Live render of <code>~/components/Footer.astro</code> in <code>BaseLayout</code>'s footer
			slot. Below the lg breakpoint (1024px) the five columns stack; above it they sit in the
			<code>1.4fr 1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr</code> grid the prototype calls for.
		</p>

		<h2 class="font-display text-h2 tracking-display mt-12">Checks</h2>
		<ul class="text-body text-ink-2 mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
			<li>
				Brand block: wordmark, description with the voice count (247), language switcher pill.
			</li>
			<li>Four link columns: The Letter / The Squad / Project / UNICEF.</li>
			<li>
				UNICEF column links open in a new tab and carry the
				<code>rel="noopener noreferrer"</code> attributes; a visually-hidden suffix announces this to
				screen readers.
			</li>
			<li>
				Stubbed links (Partners, Press, etc, plus the Privacy/Terms/Accessibility meta row) carry a
				<code>data-todo</code> attribute referencing the future issue.
			</li>
			<li>
				Language switcher opens via click and via keyboard (Enter on the pill). Escape closes it.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
